Great — I can help. First, one quick flag I noticed: the numbers you gave aren’t internally consistent, so I’ll show two reconciled views and then provide polished narrative text you can use in internal materials.

Quick reconciliation
- Cash: $5.2M (provided)
- Burn rate: $195K / month (provided)
  - If true, implied runway = 5.2M ÷ 195K = ~26.7 months
- Runway: 20 months (provided)
  - If true, implied burn = 5.2M ÷ 20 = $260K / month

Please confirm whether the 20‑month runway already includes any planned financing, committed cost reductions, or one‑time cash uses; or whether the burn rate you quoted ($195K) is an average over a period or a target burn. Also confirm whether the revenue number ($3.2M last quarter) is recognized revenue or cash collections.

Key metrics (using your inputs)
- Cash on hand: $5.2M
- Last quarter revenue: $3.2M → monthly revenue ≈ $1.067M
- If burn = $195K/month:
  - Runway ≈ 26.7 months
  - Cash burn as % of monthly revenue ≈ 18.3%
- If runway = 20 months (implied burn $260K/month):
  - Burn as % of monthly revenue ≈ 24.4%

Executive summary (short — 2–3 sentences)
- Riverfront Logistics enters the period with $5.2M of cash and strong top-line performance (Q last quarter revenue $3.2M, ~ $1.07M/month). At the current reported net burn of $195K/month, the company has a comfortable runway (~27 months). If the 20‑month runway figure is the working assumption, that implies a higher monthly net cash burn (~$260K), which raises urgency on near‑term cost/revenue actions. We recommend clarifying which burn number is operative and running a 3‑scenario cash forecast (base, downside, upside) to guide decisions on hiring, discretionary spend, and financing.

Suggested narrative for the finance pack (longer, for CFO or slide notes)
- Current position: Riverfront Logistics closed the quarter with $5.2M of cash and generated $3.2M in revenue in the quarter (avg. ~$1.07M/month). Our current net cash outflow is between $195K–$260K/month depending on whether the reported burn or the stated runway is used — we need to reconcile these inputs.
