  - Prioritize investments with clear payback and reallocate budget to highest-return growth activities.
- If runway is closer to 20 months:
  - Consider proactive conversations with potential lenders or investors to preserve optionality (no immediate raise required, but prepped).

5) Simple 12-month cash projection examples (starting cash = $5.2M)

- Scenario 1 — Base (burn = $195K/month)
  - 12-month out cash = 5.2M − 12×195K = 2.86M (runway remaining after 12 months ≈ 2.86M ÷ 195K ≈ 14.7 months)
